# VaultSpring SDLC

Use this file as a short delivery bridge. Details: [`docs/README.md`](../../docs/README.md), `docs/guides/`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `.github/pull_request_template.md`.

## Traceability (AIOS-aligned)

1. **Issue** with acceptance criteria (`.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/implementation.md`)
2. **Kickoff**: `bash scripts/task-kickoff.sh <issue> <type>/<slug>`
3. **PR** → `sandbox` (`Refs #N`), then promote → `main` (`Closes #N`)
4. **Release**: `pom.xml` + `CHANGELOG [X.Y.Z]` + annotated tag `vX.Y.Z` — see `docs/guides/releases.md`

## Git

- Semantic branch from **`sandbox`** (`feature/*`, `fix/*`, `docs/*`, `chore/*`, `ci/*`, `refactor/*`, `test/*`)
- Permanent branches: **`sandbox`** (integration) + **`main`** (releases) — [ADR-0004](../../docs/adr/0004-git-branching-strategy-sandbox.md)
- Do not force-push `main` or `sandbox`
- Commit only when the human asks

## Commits

- Format: `type: description` (Conventional Commits)
- Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `refactor`, `ci`, `chore`, `test`, `build`, `perf`
- No IDE trailers (`Co-authored-by: Cursor`, `cursoragent@cursor.com`) or “Made with Cursor” in commits/PRs
- Author: Kleilson Santos `<kleilson@icloud.com>` — see `docs/guides/attribution.md`

## Product

- Spring Boot 3.5.x / Java 17 / Maven Wrapper
- Secrets never in Git; use env vars and Vault **infrastructure** in Compose
- `CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]` for notable changes
- Docs/commits/issues: no gitmoji — [`docs/guides/writing-style.md`](docs/guides/writing-style.md)
- Do not claim MapStruct, Spring Cloud Vault, or Spring Security in docs unless they exist in `pom.xml`

## Checklist

- Issue linked in PR?
- `bash scripts/pre-push-check.sh` before push (delivery gate + CI parity)?
- Does the change match actual code, not README marketing?
- Tests green (`./mvnw -B test`) when Java is touched?
- After push: `gh pr checks --watch` — never merge on red **`issue-link`**?
- CI workflow still uses current GitHub Actions majors?
- Agent starting local Docker/JVM? Owner gave **`ok infra`** per [`docs/guides/local-runtime-authorization.md`](../../docs/guides/local-runtime-authorization.md)

## Local runtime (MacBook)

Canonical order: inspect → audit → unit tests green → **`bash scripts/pre-push-check.sh`** → **`ok infra`** (if live needed) → live proof → commit-ready → commit when owner asks → **`gh pr checks --watch`**. Three gates: task / infra / commit. Guide: [`docs/guides/local-runtime-authorization.md`](../../docs/guides/local-runtime-authorization.md) · rule: [`.cursor/rules/local-runtime-gate.mdc`](local-runtime-gate.mdc)

## PKB (prompt catalog)

- Intake: `PKB intake` / `catalogar prompt` / `guardar prompt` → [`docs/prompts/README.md`](../../docs/prompts/README.md) (catalog only until `ok` / `prossegue`; live infra still needs infra gate)
- Validate: `bash scripts/check-pkb-inventory.sh`
